# client/public/_redirects — SPA fallback for Render's static site hosting
#
# React Router handles routing entirely client-side, so there's no real
# file at a path like /dashboard — only index.html, which then loads the
# JS that renders that route. Without this file, directly loading or
# refreshing any page other than "/" 404s on Render, because the static
# host looks for a literal /dashboard file and finds nothing.
#
# Vite copies everything in client/public/ into dist/ untouched, and
# Render's static site hosting reads this exact filename (same format
# Netlify uses) — so this one rule sends every path to index.html and
# lets React Router take over from there.
/*    /index.html   200
